 "root_cause": "Download appended 206 bodies without checking offsets or completeness, accepted short responses as complete, wrote an oversized chunk before enforcing its disk bound, and registered ownership before an unguarded directory preparation.",
 "changes": [
  "Accept identity-encoded 200 full responses or validated single 206 ranges with known total length; reject invalid/unsupported range metadata before reading or appending",
  "Validate each body length and continue incomplete prefixes within the original three-request/shared-time budget rather than reporting partial success",
  "Bind known totals and strong ETags across partial responses; use If-Range and retain 200 restart behavior; weak or invalid ETags are not sent as validators",
  "Enforce declared and actual byte budgets before writing the offending chunk; reject an already oversized prefix before HTTP without truncating it",
  "Guard path preparation with the same finally retirement; preserve per-request authorization, cookies/Referer, closing behavior and sanitized errors"
 ],
